<!-- 12. Travel basics: plain teasers until the guide pages exist (Draft 4) -->
<section class="basics bg-white py-section" data-section="basics" aria-labelledby="basics-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="label text-ink-muted">Travel basics</p>
    <h2 id="basics-title" class="mt-5 text-display-lg">Before you go</h2>
    <ul class="basics-grid mt-12 md:mt-16">
      <li class="basics-card" data-basics-card>
        <p class="label text-ink-muted">01 · Weather</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-display-sm">Best time to visit Sri Lanka</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body">December to April is dry on the west and south coasts, in Colombo, Kandy and the hill country. May to September suits the east coast, including Trincomalee and Arugam Bay.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="basics-card" data-basics-card>
        <p class="label text-ink-muted">02 · Entry</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-display-sm">Visa and ETA</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body">Most visitors need an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) before travelling; some nationalities can enter visa-free. Check your passport on the official site, <a href="https://www.eta.gov.lk/" class="underline underline-offset-4" rel="noopener">eta.gov.lk</a>.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="basics-card" data-basics-card>
        <p class="label text-ink-muted">03 · Planning</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-display-sm">When to book</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body">For December to March, book two to three months ahead, as good hotels and reserved train seats sell out. Outside peak season a tour can often be arranged within a few days.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
